{
	"title": "an async generator action: a write after a `yield` is under the call's mark; a write after a plain `await` is not (nothing is open: nothing-open), and the action's promise rejects with it; a throw from a yielded promise comes back in at the yield, where it can be caught [TypeScript only: it leans on JS async generators and the order their promises settle in (microtask ticks); C has no generators, and its promises call back at once, so the order would mean nothing there. 93 has the stepping, through createWriter]",
